{"family": "unik3d", "task": "depth", "name": "UniK3D", "plain": "UniK3D: metric 3D from one image for any camera type, using a spherical-harmonic ray model. Non-commercial licence.", "summary": "UniK3D (Piccinelli et al. 2025): monocular metric 3-D for any camera model; a DINOv2 ViT-L encoder and a camera-prompted decoder predict a spherical-harmonic ray model and per-pixel radii (depth, 3-D points, confidence), or use given pinhole intrinsics.", "tier": "stable", "upstream": "https://github.com/lpiccinelli-eth/UniK3D", "upstream_commit": "29f7862", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "UniK3D: Universal Camera Monocular 3D Estimation", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.16591", "date": "2025-03-20", "venue": "CVPR 2025", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["fastbb", "dpt_fused"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "resolution_level", "default": 9, "bounds": "0 to 9", "effect": "output"}, {"name": "confidence", "default": true, "bounds": "", "effect": "output"}], "outputs": [{"name": "depth", "extra": false}, {"name": "points", "extra": false}, {"name": "confidence", "extra": false}], "output_info": {"kind": "metric"}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": [], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: a depth or inverse-depth map. `kind` (a card field, `result.kind`) says what the numbers mean: `metric` = metres; `scale_invariant`, `affine_invariant` and `affine_invariant_inverse` are relative (unknown scale or shift, not metres). Metric models that use the focal length take `model(image, intrinsics=K)` (K `[3, 3]`, pixels of the input): `metric3d-vit-large` and `da3metric-large` need it for correct metres (`da3metric-large`: metres = output x focal / 300; without `intrinsics=` a 300 px focal length is assumed, wrong for a real camera). `unidepth-v2-vitl14`, `unik3d-vitl`, `depth-pro` and MoGe estimate the camera themselves (given `intrinsics=` replace `fx`); `zoedepth-nk` and the relative models (`da3mono-large` too) take none.", "install": {"extras": ["nc"], "noncommercial_weights": ["unik3d-vitl"]}, "variants": [{"id": "unik3d-vitl", "released": "0.1.1", "added_in": "0.1.0", "ref": "unik3d-vitl@1", "name": "unik3d-vitl", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {}, "licence": {"code": "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0", "code_class": "noncommercial", "weights": "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 (assumed from code)", "weights_assumed": true, "evidence": "https://github.com/lpiccinelli-eth/UniK3D/blob/29f7862f3c3ee79c53ef0153dfc901ce511df575/LICENSE", "training_data": [{"id": "unstated", "name": "not stated by the authors"}], "training_note": "Mixture of public metric-depth datasets (pinhole, fisheye and panoramic cameras) per the UniK3D paper (arXiv 2503.16591)", "commercial": "no", "reasons": ["code: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 (noncommercial)", "weights: CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0 (assumed from code)"], "notes": ["weights licence not stated by the original authors; assumed to be the code licence", "data: unstated"]}, "weights": [{"name": "model.safetensors", "sha256": "890be79699dd68abb3c9a3aab24b528bf09d97eca4dd073e3e83c0a2028566b2", "size": 1435366192, "url": "https://huggingface.co/lpiccinelli/unik3d-vitl/resolve/008aa54308b8bc142f74c9c7b098833aaede06bd/model.safetensors", "host": "Hugging Face", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mirror": null}], "input_size": "any H x W >= 8, resized or padded inside the model (ViT patch 14)", "tested_max": {"size": "3000x4000", "alloc_mib": 2271, "reserved_mib": 2486}, "speed": {"standard": "994x1482", "inputs": [{"input": "518x770", "scene": "synthetic", "standard": false, "modes": {"original16": {"ms": 122.6, "peak_alloc_mb": 3220, "peak_reserved_mb": 3530, "scene": "synthetic (fastforks bench)", "date": "2026-11-01", "torch": "2.14.1+cu130", "protocol": "median of 5 after 3 warm-up, uint8 CUDA input, original code at the pinned co